diff --git a/docs/deployment.md b/docs/deployment.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4aff2c2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+# Deployment
+
+Fizzy ships with a [Kamal](https://kamal-deploy.org) configuration for running
+everything on a single Linux server: the Rails app and its background jobs in
+Docker containers, SQLite databases and uploaded files on a persistent volume,
+and SSL terminated by kamal-proxy with an automatically provisioned Let's
+Encrypt certificate.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- A Linux server with Docker installed and SSH access (root by default; set
+  `ssh: user:` in `config/deploy.yml` for another user).
+- A domain whose DNS points at that server. Ports 80 and 443 must be open so
+  kamal-proxy can fetch the SSL certificate.
+- An account on a container registry (Docker Hub by default, or GitHub
+  Container Registry).
+- An SMTP server to send magic sign-in links and notification emails.
+
+## Setup
+
+1. Fill in every line marked `TODO` in `config/deploy.yml`:
+   - `image` and `registry: username` — your container registry account.
+   - `servers` — your server's IP address or SSH hostname.
+   - `proxy: host` — your public hostname, e.g. `fizzy.example.com`.
+   - `env: clear` — your mail server (`SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT`,
+     `SMTP_DOMAIN`) and sender address (`MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`).
+
+2. Fill in `.kamal/secrets`:
+   - `SECRET_KEY_BASE` — generate with `bin/rails secret`.
+   - `KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD` — a registry access token.
+   - `SMTP_USERNAME` / `SMTP_PASSWORD` — your mail server credentials.
+   - `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` / `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` — optional, enables web push
+     notifications. Generate a pair with:
+
+     ```sh
+     bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}\nVAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+     ```
+
+3. Deploy:
+
+   ```sh
+   bin/kamal setup
+   ```
+
+   Kamal builds the image, pushes it to your registry, boots kamal-proxy with
+   SSL, runs the migrations, and starts the app and its background job worker.
+   Fizzy comes up at `https://<your host>`.
+
+4. Open `https://<your host>` and sign up. The sign-in code arrives by email,
+   so your mail server needs to work for this step.
+
+## Day to day
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy   # build, push, and roll out a new version
+bin/kamal console  # Rails console on the server
+bin/kamal app logs # tail the app logs
+```
+
+Your data — the SQLite databases and uploaded files — lives in the
+`fizzy-storage` Docker volume mounted at `/rails/storage`, so it survives
+deploys. Remember to back it up:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal app exec 'tar czf - -C /rails storage' > fizzy-backup.tar.gz
+```
